# Testing Standards

## Test Framework
- Use pytest with markers for be, integration, e2e, and perf
- Generate tests when behaviour changes
- Add type checks (pyright or mypy) and keep hints/recommendations compatible

## Test Strategy
- For any non-trivial change, propose/adjust tests first
- Keep coverage thresholds and fail-under respected
- Do not disable linters/tests to "make it pass"
- Fix root causes or clearly justify in the PR text

## Test Planning
- When proposing refactors, output a minimal test plan and risk notes
- Default to safe refactors (rename, extract, inline) with explicit before/after behaviour notes
- Use checklists for risky edits: migration steps, rollback, and verification